  "prefLabel": "Mavs 203.04 Computation of Time Periods",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mavs 203.04 Computation of Time Periods. In computing any period of time prescribed or allowed by these rules:\n\n(a) The first day of the period shall be the day after the act or event which the designated period of time begins; and\n\n(b) The last day of the period so computed shall be included unless it is a Saturday, Sunday, or state legal holiday, in which event the period shall extend until the end of the next day that is not a Saturday, Sunday, or state legal holiday as specified in RSA 288.\n\nSource. #13459-A, eff 10-14-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mavs200.html"
